    ('KB', "w|sky+blue|Air scatters blue light more than red, so the sky looks blue.\nw|sunset+red sunset+orange|At sunset light crosses more air. Blue scatters away, leaving red.\nw|sea+salty ocean+salty sea+salt ocean+salt|Rivers wash minerals into the sea, and water evaporates, leaving salt.\nw|grass+green leaf+green plant+green|Chlorophyll reflects green light and soaks up red and blue.\nw|leaf+fall leaf+change autumn+color fall+color|In fall chlorophyll fades, showing yellow and orange pigments.\nw|moon+shape moon+phase moon+change|We see different sunlit parts of the Moon as it orbits Earth.\nw|tide|The Moon's gravity tugs on the oceans and makes the tides."),
    ('KB', "w|season summer+winter|Earth's axis is tilted, so sunlight hits us at different angles.\nw|night+dark night+come|Our side of Earth turns away from the Sun, so it gets dark.\nw|thunder lightning|Lightning heats air so fast it booms. That's thunder!\nw|rainbow|Raindrops split sunlight into colors, making a rainbow.\nw|ice+float|Ice is less dense than liquid water, so it floats.\nw|star+twinkle|Air bends starlight, making stars seem to twinkle.\nw|dinosaur+extinct dinosaur+die dinosaur+gone|A huge asteroid hit Earth about 66 million years ago.\nw|yawn|Nobody is sure. Yawning may cool the brain or boost alertness.\nw|hiccup|Your diaphragm spasms and your vocal cords snap shut. Hic!"),
    ('KB', "w|cat+purr|Cats purr when happy, and also to soothe themselves.\nw|dog+tail|Tail wags show excitement. The speed and direction show mood.\nw|sleep+need sleep+important|Sleep helps your body heal and your brain store memories.\nw|dream|Your brain sorts memories during REM sleep, and that's dreaming.\nw|onion+cry onion+tear|Cut onions release a gas that irritates your eyes.\nw|brain+freeze|Cold hits your palate and nerves send a quick head pain.\nw|finger+wrinkle|Wet fingers wrinkle to give you a better grip on slippery things.\nw|zebra+stripe|Stripes may confuse biting flies and help keep zebras cool.\nw|bird+migrate bird+south bird+winter|Birds migrate to find food and warmer weather."),
